        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "‘Stella Maris – Steps from The Burrow’s Sandy Shores’\r\n\r\nKehoe & Assoc. together with Claude Howlin Auctioneers are delighted to present Stella Maris, an impressive and character-filled detached residence occupying a mature site of c.  0.51 acres in the highly regarded coastal setting of The Burrow, Rosslare Strand.\r\n\r\nThe original residence dates from 1977, with a substantial extension completed in 2007, creating a wonderfully spacious family home extending to c. 233 sq.m. The property has evolved considerably over the years while retaining the charm and character associated with the original dwelling. Generous living accommodation, mature private grounds and a substantial detached garage combine to create a particularly appealing property in one of County Wexford’s most established coastal locations.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is entered through a welcoming entrance hallway and offers an excellent balance of formal and informal living space. There is a comfortable sitting room and separate dining room, while at the heart of the home lies a particularly spacious kitchen featuring a handmade bespoke timber kitchen with central island. Double doors lead from here into the large family room, creating an excellent space for everyday family living and entertaining.\r\n\r\nA bright sunroom enjoys an attractive outlook over the rear gardens and provides a peaceful connection between the house and its mature outdoor setting. Completing the principal living accommodation are a practical utility room and separate shower room.\r\n\r\nThe ground-floor bedroom accommodation comprises three bedrooms, each fitted with built-in wardrobes, together with a family bathroom. This arrangement provides considerable flexibility and makes Stella Maris particularly suitable for those seeking predominantly single-level living.\r\nAt first-floor level, the converted attic provides substantial additional accommodation, presently arranged to include a lounge area, office and extensive ancillary space. This level offers considerable versatility for home working, hobbies, recreation or additional storage. Subject to the necessary planning permission and building regulations, there may also be potential to further enhance this area, including the possibility of incorporating dormer windows to the rear and developing additional bedroom accommodation.\r\n\r\nExternally, Stella Maris is equally impressive. The property occupies a generally level and mature site extending to c. 0.51 acres, approached via a private driveway and surrounded by established landscaped gardens laid predominantly in lawn. To the rear is an enclosed concrete courtyard together with further lawned gardens, creating a private and sheltered outdoor setting with ample space for relaxation, entertaining and family use.\r\n\r\nA particularly noteworthy feature is the large, detached garage, complete with a loft area above and electrical supply. Currently providing excellent workshop, storage and ancillary accommodation, the building also presents interesting potential for alternative uses or future development, subject to the relevant planning permission.\r\n\r\nLocation:\r\n\r\nStella Maris enjoys an enviable position at The Burrow, Rosslare Strand, only 2 km from Rosslare Strand Village and 18 km south-east of Wexford Town. The Burrow is a long-established and highly regarded coastal setting, particularly prized for its natural landscape, proximity to the sea and relaxed residential character.\r\n\r\nThe property is conveniently accessed from The Burrow Road, providing easy connectivity with Rosslare Strand Village and the wider south County Wexford road network. Rosslare Strand is renowned as both a permanent residential location and one of the county’s most popular seaside destinations, with its extensive sandy beach, coastal walks and excellent range of recreational amenities.\r\n\r\nThe village provides an excellent selection of everyday services including shops, cafés, restaurants, public houses, medical facilities and community amenities, together with a primary school, church and hotels. The renowned Rosslare Golf Club is also close at hand, while the beautiful beach and picturesque walks along The Burrow offer exceptional opportunities to enjoy this unique coastal environment.\r\n\r\nRosslare Strand also benefits from rail and bus connections, while Rosslare Europort, one of Ireland’s principal passenger and freight ferry terminals, is conveniently accessible, providing regular connections with Britain and continental Europe.\r\n\r\nWexford Town is within comfortable driving distance and offers an extensive range of shopping, restaurants, schools, healthcare, sporting and recreational facilities.\r\n\r\nStella Maris represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial and characterful coastal home on mature private grounds, combining generous accommodation, considerable ancillary space and further potential in the highly sought-after setting of The Burrow, Rosslare Strand.\r\nIt is highly recommended, to arrange a suitable viewing time, please contact selling agents, Kehoe & Assoc., at 053 9144393 or Claude Howlin Auctioneers at 053 9147949."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Storm Porch\t1.22m x 0.74m\tConcrete step leading through to double glazed pvc door.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway\t3.99m x 1.62m\tCarpeted flooring, coving.\r\n\r\nDoor leading through to:\r\n\r\nFront Sitting Room\t4.54m x 3.44m\tCarpeted flooring, large pvc double glazed window overlooking front garden, tv points and electrical points, feature fireplace with open stove, granite tile surround and bespoke handmade oak timber mantelpiece, coving throughout.\r\n\r\nAcross Hall:\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\t4.55m x 3.45m\tCarpeted flooring, large pvc double glazed window overlooking front driveway and entrance gate with sea views, four bay built in wardrobes with recess lights and coving trim, ample storage with drawer, shelving and rails.\r\n\r\nCentral Corridor leading to further accommodation areas:\r\n\r\nCentral Corridor\t4.66m x 0.90m\tCarpeted flooring and coving.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\t3.45m x 3.03m\tCarpeted flooring, double glazed pvc window overlooking rear courtyard, double bay built in wardrobe with open shelf display, tv points and electrical points.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\t2.71m x 2.38m\tCarpeted flooring, built in wardrobes with overhead storage, double glazed pvc window overlooking rear courtyard.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom\t2.36m x 1.79m\tTiled flooring, floor to ceiling tile surround, recess lights, bath with Myra Elite SE electric pump shower overhead, w.h.b with mirror and lighting overhead and w.c, built in cabinetry for further storage.\r\n\r\nFrom Central Hallway, glass door leading through to:\r\n\r\nDining Room\t3.43m x 2.98m\tTimber engineered flooring, coving with feature stone cladded wall, privacy glass leading out to sunroom area, wall insert gas fire.\r\n\r\nOpen alcove leading through to:\r\n\r\nKitchen/Living Space\t7.73m x 5.02m\tTiled flooring throughout, stone cladded feature wall, fully fitted kitchen bespokely made elm kitchen, floor and eye level cabinets through with separate island and work station space, granite worktops throughout, double stainless steel sink and granite stone cut drainer, 100mm uprise granite stone surround and granite windowsill, recess lights built in throughout the kitchen, the appliances include Bosch  integrated fridge, Bosch integrated double oven, Bosch integrated microwave, Bosch integrated four ring electric hob with extractor fan overhead, integrated Bosch dishwasher and ample drawer and storage space with display cabinetry and wine rack, pendant lights over the breakfast counter area with recess electric panel and raised glass table structure.\r\n\r\nDouble glazed pvc doors leading through to:\r\n\r\nSunroom\t3.30m (max) x 3.39m (max)\tTimber laminate flooring with pedestrian door access leading out through rear courtyard.\r\n\r\nFrom Kitchen, door leading through to:\r\n\r\nUtility Space\t3.09m x 2.03m\tTiled flooring throughout, Bosch washing machine and Bosch dishwasher, floor to ceiling built in cabinetry, granite worktop leading into the feature corner window overlooking the courtyard. Hot-press with insulated tank and open shelves.\r\n\r\nDoor leading through to:\r\n\r\nShower Room\t2.00m x 1.84m\tTiled flooring, floor to ceiling tile surround, mosaic tile with stainless steel drainer, pressure pump shower, w.h.b with mirror and lighting built in overhead, chrome towel rail and w.c.\r\n\r\nFrom the Kitchen, double doors leading to:\r\n\r\nFamily Lounge\t5.07m x 4.91m\tCarpeted flooring throughout, feature bay window with five bay aspect overlooking front garden with trees and sea view to the rear of those trees, built in tv console station with granite worktop and ample storage and drawers underneath tv points and electrical points, recess lights.\r\n\r\nFrom the Kitchen is a solid oak carpeted staircase leading to the converted attic:\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n \t\t\r\nOpen Plan Play Area/Storage Area\t6.88m x 6.67m\tCarpeted flooring throughout, electrical points, recess lights, two pockets for storage in the eaves, window with Venetian blind.\r\n\r\nTo the left of the stairs, doorway leading through to:\r\n\r\nHome Office Area:\t6.85m x 2.51m\tCarpeted flooring, built in storage throughout with ample workstation space, double glazed pvc window with Venetian blind overlooking central courtyard.\r\n\r\nFrom the T open area, door leading through to:\r\n\r\nCorridor Entrance\t1.27m x 1.06m\tCarpeted flooring.\r\n\r\nAncillary Room\t8.12m x 1.12m\tCarpeted flooring throughout, four Velux overhead with ample light, built in workstation, tv console and storage, built in closet to the eave.\r\n\r\nTotal Floor Area: c. 233 sq.m / 2,508 sq.ft"
